+
+## Level packs (LV8, plan 8.8)
+
+A level that `mapc` compiled can be delivered as one **pack**. The PS1 and the Dreamcast read the 24 new levels from `BREACH.BIN` on
+the disc; the GBA keeps its 7 as const ROM data. Source of truth: `core/include/doomo/breachpack.h` (byte layout and API), the writer
+`tools/packbreach.py`, the reader `core/src/breachpack.c`.
+
+* **Format `BRPK` v1**, little endian, every field written and read one by one (no struct copy: pointer sizes differ between the host,
+  the MIPS and the SH4). Header 80 B (magic, version 1, 12 sections, total length, crc32 of bytes 16..end, then w, h, kind, sky, music,
+  ambient, the `MAPX_*` flags, fog, view, gravity, note, `detail[3]`, hero look / loadout, the counts, the title as the name), then a
+  table of 12 sections of 16 B (id, encoding raw / LZ, offset, stored length, raw length). Sections, each 4-aligned: cells (8 B each; LZ
+  with the save / PS1 codec of `ps1/tools/packart.py` when that is smaller), things (6), tflags2 (1 per thing or none), zones (7), paths
+  (6), path points (2), swap sets (6), swap cells (10), script bytes, text, texture bank, sprite bank. The **text** section is `u16`
+  count, `u16` offsets, then NUL-terminated strings (the level's strings, from an optional `NAME.strings` next to the map, at most 64,
+  4 KB). The **texture bank** section is the 12-byte names of the ids 56.. (`texbank N NAME`; empty = unused id), then the `LVTB` blob of
+  `tools/texbank.py` unchanged (`core/data/texbanks/NAME.bank` for the map NAME; id 56 + k answers from slot k, so a named id must be
+  that slot: the writer and `bp_open` refuse anything else). The **sprite bank** section is reserved for LV7b and empty in v1.
+* **Limits.** A pack is at most 96 KB; what the reader keeps resident (tables + text, `bp_tables_bytes`) at most 12 KB; things at most
+  256; the other counts are the `DOOMO_*` limits of `map.h`. `packbreach.py` and the reader both refuse a pack over them.
+* **Reader** (`breachpack.h`; no allocation, no static state, state lives in the caller's `BpLevel` and arena): `bp_head` validates the
+  header and the section table (magic, version, section count, every section inside the pack, no overlap, every length equal to its
+  count, counts over their limits, fields in range); `bp_crc_check` / `bp_open` check the crc; `bp_load` (memory, host and Dreamcast) and
+  `bp_load_mode` (any `BpRead` callback: CD sectors on the PS1) fill a `DoomoMapDef` + `DoomoMapExt` whose pointers lie in the arena
+  (cells decoded into the arena, into a caller's buffer, or left packed as `LZMC` for the PS1); `bp_bin_load` does the directory, the
+  header, the crc and the load for a level id of a `BREACH.BIN`. Contents are checked while they are copied (a thing, zone, path point
+  or swap cell outside the map, an unknown zone / path / swap kind, a bad text table are refused). Every refusal has a test
+  (`core/tests/test_breachpack.c`: short, magic, version, section out of range, overlap, counts over the limits, bad crc and a flipped
+  byte anywhere, wrong sizes, bad encodings, a corrupt LZ stream, small or misaligned arena, failing reads, bad directory).
+* **`BREACH.BIN`**: sector 0 is the directory (`BRBN`, version, count, total length, then up to 24 entries of level id, platform mask,
+  offset, length, crc; the crc is the pack's own), then every pack on a 2048-byte sector. `python3 tools/packbreach.py [--platform
+  ps1|dc] --out-dir DIR | --bin FILE [--check] [MAP.txt ...]`: with no map it packs the levels of the manifest whose map file exists;
+  `--check` rebuilds everything in memory, reads each pack back with the independent Python reader and compares it to the mapc model.
+* **Manifest** `core/data/maps/platforms.txt`: `level ID [map=NAME] [gba yes|no] [ps1 yes|no] [dc yes|no]` (defaults gba no, ps1 yes,
+  dc yes). The 24 lines are the plan's HB8-HB16 and N1-N15; the 7 of plan 7.1 (HB8, HB9, HB13, HB15, N1, N7, N14) are `gba yes`. The
+  line's index is the **level id** in `BREACH.BIN` (default chosen by Claude (LEVELS-2), owner may override; the LV0 registry maps its own ids
+  to it). `map=NAME` names the map file once a level has a real name; a line without a map file is skipped. `gba yes` here and in the
+  map's header must agree (`packbreach.py --check`). `mapc` wraps the generated file of a manifest level in `#if
+  !defined(DOOMO_PLATFORM_PS1) [&& !defined(DOOMO_PLATFORM_GBA)]`: the PS1 never links the const data (it uses the pack) and the GBA links
+  it only with `gba yes`. The 12 shipped maps are not in the manifest and their generated files are byte for byte what they were
+  (`make -C core check-gen`).
+* **PS1** (`ps1/src/breachdisc.c`, docs/PS1.md "LV8"): reader and loader are code of the combat + levels overlay group
+  (`ovl_plan.py`: `breach(pack|disc)`), never resident; the level lives in the core's 12 KB scene scratch block; the cells stay packed
+  as `LZMC` and `map_def_cells()` decodes them into the live map; the texture bank's frame 0 is uploaded to the pinned slots 72..79.
+  Option `-DDOOMO_BREACH_BIN=ON` (default OFF until a first new level exists).
+* **Dreamcast** (`dc/src/breachdisc.c`): `plat_breach_level(id, &def, &ext)` reads `/cd/BREACH.BIN` through the KOS file calls and the
+  core reader (`make -C dc BREACH=1`); the bank is activated with `texbank_activate`. Host test: `make -C dc check-breachdisc` (part of
+  `make dc-host-test`). The on-hardware step (a pack from a real GD-ROM on Flycast or a console) waits for the first new level: there is
+  nothing to load yet.
+* **GBA** (`gba/tools/memreport.py`): the manifest decides what the GBA build compiles; `make -C gba` prints `levels ROM` (map tables of
+  the maps the build carries, from `tools/levelcheck.py`) and `levels EWRAM / IWRAM` (the levels objects in the linker map; the pack
+  reader is linked out of the ROM).
+* **Not here:** the sprite bank content, songs, any new level, animated bank frames on the PS1 (frame 0 only), the level select calling
+  `plat_breach_level` (LV0 / the first level package).
